  "question": {
    "text": "Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>t</mi></mfenced></math> denote the greatest integer <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>t</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mi>t</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;denote the fractional part of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math>. Then integral value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math>&nbsp;for which the left hand limit of the function <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>&#945;</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mrow></mfrac></math>&nbsp;at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;is equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;is _____",
    "image": null
  },
